    "group": "201-300",
    "title": "Product of Array Except Self",
    "workload": "generate 8 arrays of 100000 values drawn from {-1,1} once, then 400 punches of the two-sweep prefix/suffix pass. Values are bounded because the algorithm multiplies a running product across the whole array and arbitrary values overflow i64 within ~20 elements -- kara traps overflow by default, so the bench would abort rather than measure. Zeros are excluded so the sink discriminates: with zeros present a 100000-element draw contains two with near-certainty, zeroing every output and collapsing the sink to 0. Values come from LCG bit 16, not bit 0, because a power-of-two-modulus LCG has period 2 in its low bit. Sink is position-weighted mod 1e9+7.",
    "sink": "-331405379"
